{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048312-2ed-adapting-the-walkers-in-mists","id":1048312,"title":"[2ed] Adapting the Walkers in Mists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-13T10:40:42-08:00","id":1048312,"title":"[2ed] Adapting the Walkers in Mists","content":"Hello people. I'm trying to adapt the old Walkers in the Mist to the 2ed.<br /> I would appreciate some help with the Yantras, Initiation and the Attainments. I made up the first one. And don't know ir the second one(adapted from the 1st one on 1ed) is working the same way.<br /> <br /> So far, I'm thinking about something among these lines:<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Space 2, Occult 2, Survival 2<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> A potential Druid will travel inside an Enigmatic Gate for a week. The prospect needs to cast Space 1 \u2018Correspondence\u2019 and discover the Key. The Gate will be one already visited by his Mentor and may or may not be dangerous.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic</b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Space<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Using an appropriate plant (+1); Reading bones or dices (+1); Drawing a trail (+2).<br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Trailblazing; Orienteering; A ceremony performed within an Ancient Ruin.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> To truly walk the Mists, the mage who learns this Legacy needs to be proficient in the Mysteries of Life and Space. These attainments work best in natural environments or in places of ancient power. Since most Walkers come from the Acanthus Path, they are also expected to know the Mysteries of Fate and chance, although these aren\u2019t required for their attainments.<br /> <br /> <b>1st Attainment: <i>Walking the Mists</i><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation</b><br /> This power works as <i>\u2018Ground-Eater\u2019 </i>spell, increasing the speed of the Druid equal to his dots on the Space Arcana. You can turn this effect on and off with an instant action.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Mind 2</b><br /> The druid can make his walk appear normal to those who witness him.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Attainment: <i>Peer into the Mists</i><br /> Prerequisites: Life 1, Space 2, Occult 3</b><br /> The mage peers into the Mists, the continuum of Nature that lies hidden behind the mundane world, hidden even from the Mage Sight. Doing so allows him to scry into distant places as if he were using the <i>\u2018</i><i>Scrying\u2019 </i>spell. He must scry through the medium of plant life \u2014 trees, flowers, bushes or even grass. As long as there is some form of plant life in the place he wishes to scry, the mage can see there. This roll is modified by the sympathetic distance between the plants. After he has established the window, a reflexive action is required to view through it.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: Time 2</b><br /> the mage also has Time 2, he can peer into the past at the location he is scrying, similar to the <i>\u201cPostcognition\u201d</i> spell. He literally speaks to plants to get their memory of events viewed. He can view the past only if the plants currently present at the location were there during the time the mage wishes to view.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:06:29-08:00","id":1048368,"title":"","content":"Optional Attainments should try to stick with just one Arcana just like the primary attainments do. Also, the Mistwalkers really have no need to hide Ground Eater (Good choice for 1st attainment by the way).<br /> <br /> Not sure the Sympathy works for the 2nd attainment. The idea is right, but I think the exact wording isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T14:52:16-08:00","id":1048431,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about having another additional arcana (life 1) that isn't one of the paths/legacy's ruling arcana as a prerequisite for the non-optional 2nd attainment. Considering the other necessity of having occult 3, this feels like a significant exp tax especially in light that the use of the scrying window is dependent of the presence of plant life and so is narrower than the standard scrying spell. If the attainment was broader in scope or more powerful then i could maybe understand the additional requirement but this is not the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":865,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","user":"WelshBoi","date":". 02-13-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T02:44:02-08:00","id":1048644,"title":"","content":"The primary Attainments should be based on Space. Being Achantus, the Optional Attainments have to use one of their Path Ruling. I recommend Time. <br /> <br /> I would base their Attainments around their connection to the Mists, a Space-Time Emanation realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T08:58:41-08:00","id":1048767,"title":"","content":"The initial Walkers were all about scrying and finding ways through mazes. Finding directions and traveling to remote locations (likely to find Time Before stuff, they ARE mystagog aligned after all). I'm not feeling the first attainment's effect of walking fast. I'd sooner go with Correspondance (find something interesting, start following it back home) or Locate Object (never get lost or lose things). I'd also recommend keeping to Time and drop the Mind. I'd use Momentary Flux as a level 1 optional attainment. <br /> <br /> I personally would just drop the Life / plant bits. &quot;Talking&quot; with stone pillars should be just as valid as talking with trees.<br /> <br /> <br /> Especially in light of Dark Eras, I almost feel like you'd be better off going with Mastigos as a base and learning Time. Traveling through mazes that you can get lost in, including forests, is more of a Mastigos thing thing now, rather than Acanthus. Acanthus are the ones who are all about guiding destiny in some way. Personally, I feel like that Path just doesn't fit the Walkers anymore. Originally it was probably tied to Acanthus because of the whole Celtic-Fae thing being all Acanthus-y, but if we ignore the fae angle, and just go on the themes of the past, the Walkers are all about finding paths and being guides and explorers than anything related to destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T09:32:59-08:00","id":1048782,"title":"","content":"@MCN they study a &quot;nature beyond nature&quot; that they believe is guiding the destiny of the natural world. Hence Acanthus with Space primary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T18:34:05-08:00","id":1049071,"title":"","content":"My take on them:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Walkers in Mists</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Origins</span> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Acanthus, Mysterium<br /> <b>Background</b>: The Legacy has traditionally recruited members from those of Celtic descent, especially those who have at least a passing knowledge in the old druidic customs. However, as the modern world narrow their niche and their numbers dwindle, elder Druids have started to look for prospective pupils among non-Celtic peoples that display talents in pathfinding or divination, and those who enjoy traveling untraveled roads.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Druids prefer practical and casual garments suited for long times of outdoor activity. Backpacks are common, and so are hiking and camping equipment. In formal gatherings, they wear druidic robes embellished with Celtic accessories.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Doctrine</span> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Space 2, Survival 2, two dots in one of the following Skills; Academics, Occult, Medicine, Expression, Streetwise<br /> Initiation: The prospective member must travel seven days and seven nights, relying solely on mundane means that he has on his person at the start of the journey. He must not revisit the same location, but otherwise is free to design her course and destination. Once the journey is over, the mentor leads him inside an Iris into the Mists to recognize him as a member among other members of the Legacy. While this initiation has traditionally taken place in the countrysides where there are no developed roads, modern day Walkers have decided to relax this convention, and in some cases even allow city-walking.<br /> <b>Organization</b>: While many Druids go on journeys alone or in small groups, they are also expected to eventually return to society and share their wisdom and knowledge. They tend to set up headquarters of a sort, where Druids may return to for rest and sharing knowledge. A typical mentor figure settles in one of such centers and teaches several students about the Legacy's magical lore.<br /> <b>Theory</b>: There is a place and time, distant from that of ours, where destiny unfolds itself in the form of hazy fog. This is a nature beyond nature, a sort of &quot;supernature&quot;, that is connected to the world through secret trods and fairy circles. The voices of the gods can be heard when walking these hidden paths and in the games of chance, both of which the world has long forgotten their purpose.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magic</span> <br /> <b>R</b><b>uling Arcanum</b>: Space<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Using dice, runes, or other games of chance in a divination (+1), tools made of consecrated wood (+1), large stone monuments and ruins (+2)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Carving runes or ogham letters into wood or stone, sharing knowledge about secret passages, meditating amidst a lit herbal incense<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attainments</span><br /> <br /> <b>At the Edge of the Paths</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation<br /> The Druid trains to familiarize herself with the hidden paths of nature. With this Attainment, her Peripheral Mage Sight now picks up the presence of Irises. Aberrances, which connect to the Abyss, do not fall under this Attainment's domain.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 1<br /> By tracing the secret roads, the Druid is now unerred by the vagaries of time in his travels. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Green Light / Red Light&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use. It is used solely to smoothe the mage's own movements. When used within the Mists, the Attainment also gains advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Striding the Paths</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Space 2, Survival 3<br /> The Druid learns to move quickly along the paths to reach her destination. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Ground-Eater&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced Duration. The Attainment is used solely to enhance the mage's own Speed.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 2<br /> The Druid looks ahead the path to roughly determine where it leads to. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Momentary Flux&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use and sensory range. The visions come in floral and wooden scents, with fresh fragrance representing good tidings and rotting stench signifying ill omens. When used within the Mists, the Attainment also gains advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Entering the Mists</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Space 3, two dots in a second Skill among initiation list<br /> Experienced Druids are entitled to enter the Mists, the Emanation of Unknown Destiny. The mage may now enter an existing Thura to the Mists without fulfilling its Keys. She also negates Paradox risk of Space spells within the realm, in addition to Time magic.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 3<br /> The Druid's contact with the Mists allow him to peer into the future even in the material realm. This Attainment replicates the &quot; Divination&quot; spell. Reach is assigned to instant use, sensory range, and enabling detailed questions and answers. When used within the Mists, the mage may use this Attainment in conjunction with the Sympathetic Range Attainment, but without expending Reach to access sensory range beforehand.<br /> <br /> <b>Where the Paths Cross</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Space 4, Survival 4<br /> The Druid calls forth the rolling fog of the Mists into physical space, using its properties to blur distance as it blurs time. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Co-Location&quot; spell, with the resultant areas appearing to be covered in thick mist. Reach is assigned to sensory range and advanced Duration. Also, the mage may assign a number of pre-set locations equal to her Space dots to use this Attainment in conjunction with the Sympathetic Range Attainment.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 4<br /> The occult principle of crossing into distant places now extend to crossing into distant futures. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Present as Past&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to instant use. Should this provoke a Clash of Wills, the mage gains automatic successes equal to her Time dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Inviting the Mists</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Space 5, two dots in a third Skill among initiation list<br /> The eldest of Druids walk so closely with the nature beyond nature, that it now walks with her at all times. The mage may create a Thura into the Mists in her demesne. She may assign a Key to it either on moment of creation, or whenever she wishes later. Destroying either the demesne or the Thura destroys the other.<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Time 5<br /> The Mists fill the Druid's eyes and hands, allowing him to briefly dictate the path in front of him. This Attainment replicates the &quot;Prophecy&quot; spell, with Reach assigned to sensory range. When used within the Mists, the mage may use this Attainment as if he had assigned Reach to instant use, and in conjuction with the Sympathetic Range Attainment without expending Reach to access sensory range beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T03:37:32-08:00","id":1049209,"title":"","content":"I think Postcognition and Ban should be worked in there somewhere like they had in 1e. Anyway, an Emanation has an Iris at the center, but the area surrounding it is also effected. I see the Mists probably emanating from one Iris at the center of an Emanation but they manage to creep all over the world, they just get diffused to the merest wisps that members of the legacy specialize in noticing. Space would be the arcana for moving through the Mists and Time would be the arcana for seeing where you've been and where you're going. Alternatively, the Mists inside the Emanation realm can potentially drop you anywhere/when and the Space attainments are mainly tooled to getting you back to the Emanation faster so you can strike out again while the Time attainments pretty much keep doing what they're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T10:59:13-08:00","id":1049373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1048312-2ed-adapting-the-walkers-in-mists?p=1049071#post1049071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on them:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Walkers in Mists</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I, FU**ING LOVED IT!!!<br /> <br /> Thank you sir.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}